  "title": "Sony brings AI upscaling to the regular PS5",
  "narration": "Sony just gave the regular PS5 an AI graphics upgrade. Until now, PlayStation's PSSR upscaler was locked to PS5 Pro because it was too heavy for the base console. Sony's workaround is QSSR — a smaller neural network, hand-tuned for the original PS5. It should sharpen detail and reduce image shimmer, with Marvel's Wolverine and Ghost of Yōtei among the first games getting it. Here's the catch: PSSR on PS5 Pro still looks better. So your five-year-old console just learned a new trick. It still isn't a Pro, but it's definitely trying.",
